1
00:00:00,022 --> 00:00:01,816
Welcome to ResGrid Academy.

2
00:00:01,982 --> 00:00:06,205
In this lesson, we will configure
a department and protect access.

3
00:00:06,407 --> 00:00:10,831
Wrong time zones distort schedules,
and broad permissions expose work

4
00:00:10,831 --> 00:00:12,538
to people who do not need it.

5
00:00:12,682 --> 00:00:16,398
We will explain the features,
the setup decisions, and a

6
00:00:16,398 --> 00:00:18,510
practical way to check the result.

7
00:00:19,328 --> 00:00:24,293
An administrator sets the department
time zone, hides modules the department

8
00:00:24,305 --> 00:00:28,869
will not use, requires two-factor
sign-in for administrators and adds

9
00:00:28,872 --> 00:00:32,891
a second administrator, sets the
time zone and address everything

10
00:00:32,891 --> 00:00:37,299
else uses, and keeps administrative
access limited and recoverable.

11
00:00:37,474 --> 00:00:41,447
The examples in this series use a
fictional department and are teaching

12
00:00:41,447 --> 00:00:43,894
scenarios, not default settings.

13
00:00:44,697 --> 00:00:49,454
Department settings, department
address, time zone, and core settings.

14
00:00:49,688 --> 00:00:51,797
Confirm the address and time zone.

15
00:00:52,016 --> 00:00:54,992
Dates, maps, and schedules depend on them.

16
00:00:55,814 --> 00:00:56,978
Module settings.

17
00:00:57,205 --> 00:01:00,301
Turn optional modules on
or off for the department.

18
00:01:00,504 --> 00:01:04,182
Hide modules you will not use
so members see a simpler menu.

19
00:01:04,986 --> 00:01:05,723
Permissions.

20
00:01:05,947 --> 00:01:09,212
Who can create calls, see
personal information, and

21
00:01:09,213 --> 00:01:11,224
perform other sensitive actions?

22
00:01:11,423 --> 00:01:12,759
Review each permission.

23
00:01:12,981 --> 00:01:14,697
Some default to every member.

24
00:01:15,477 --> 00:01:17,245
Two-factor authentication.

25
00:01:17,477 --> 00:01:19,890
Two-factor sign-in for member accounts.

26
00:01:20,091 --> 00:01:23,175
Enroll every administrator
in two-factor sign-in.

27
00:01:24,039 --> 00:01:26,077
Security and session policy.

28
00:01:26,268 --> 00:01:30,226
Two-factor requirements, password
rules, and session limits.

29
00:01:30,428 --> 00:01:33,893
Require two-factor sign-in
for administrators and review

30
00:01:33,911 --> 00:01:35,607
password and session rules.

31
00:01:36,473 --> 00:01:38,351
Single sign-on and provisioning.

32
00:01:38,565 --> 00:01:42,420
Let members sign in through your
identity provider with optional

33
00:01:42,420 --> 00:01:44,247
automatic account provisioning.

34
00:01:44,458 --> 00:01:48,342
Know your department address and
time zone and choose at least two

35
00:01:48,342 --> 00:01:50,544
people who will administer ResGrid.

36
00:01:51,345 --> 00:01:52,220
Audit history.

37
00:01:52,446 --> 00:01:55,032
See who changed department
settings and when.

38
00:01:55,235 --> 00:01:59,119
Know your department address and
time zone and choose at least two

39
00:01:59,119 --> 00:02:01,324
people who will administer ResGrid.

40
00:02:02,145 --> 00:02:03,908
Account sessions and recovery.

41
00:02:04,062 --> 00:02:07,981
Your own sign-in sessions,
password and two-factor settings.

42
00:02:08,189 --> 00:02:12,073
Know your department address and
time zone and choose at least two

43
00:02:12,073 --> 00:02:14,277
people who will administer ResGrid.

44
00:02:15,113 --> 00:02:16,670
Setup help and support.

45
00:02:16,901 --> 00:02:20,159
Setup wizard, setup
report, and admin assist.

46
00:02:20,335 --> 00:02:24,220
Know your department address and
time zone and choose at least two

47
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:26,431
people who will administer ResGrid.

48
00:02:27,243 --> 00:02:31,253
Passkeys add a device-backed sign-in
factor and need deliberate naming,

49
00:02:31,425 --> 00:02:33,684
removal, and recovery handling.

50
00:02:33,878 --> 00:02:37,664
Enroll from Account Security
on a compatible demo device.

51
00:02:37,870 --> 00:02:41,506
Name the credential and review
the remaining recovery factors.

52
00:02:41,697 --> 00:02:44,844
Confirm an actual sign-in
and check the credential list

53
00:02:44,846 --> 00:02:46,569
after a controlled removal.

54
00:02:46,772 --> 00:02:49,778
Confirm availability in
the demo department before

55
00:02:49,780 --> 00:02:51,432
recording the live workflow.

56
00:02:52,281 --> 00:02:55,170
For the training scenario,
work in this order.

57
00:02:55,396 --> 00:02:59,150
Step one, confirm the department
address and time zone.

58
00:02:59,403 --> 00:03:02,647
Step two, choose the modules
the department will use

59
00:03:02,648 --> 00:03:03,955
and review permissions.

60
00:03:04,201 --> 00:03:07,936
Step three, enroll two
administrators in MFA before

61
00:03:07,936 --> 00:03:10,015
reviewing enforcement and recovery.

62
00:03:10,797 --> 00:03:12,435
Now verify the result.

63
00:03:12,628 --> 00:03:16,090
Use separate administrator and
member accounts to check allowed

64
00:03:16,090 --> 00:03:18,024
actions and resource visibility.

65
00:03:18,229 --> 00:03:21,737
Test recovery before enforcing
stricter sign-in rules.

66
00:03:21,939 --> 00:03:25,550
A common problem to watch
for, hiding a module is not

67
00:03:25,550 --> 00:03:27,886
evidence that API access stops.

68
00:03:28,106 --> 00:03:32,332
MFA enrollment is separate from a
tested factor and recovery path.

69
00:03:33,103 --> 00:03:34,934
Your practice task is simple.

70
00:03:35,125 --> 00:03:39,984
Complete setup wizard, save on each
owning screen, then verify again.

71
00:03:40,197 --> 00:03:43,586
Keep unknown checks visible
and assign follow-up owners.

72
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:48,300
Record the result, who owns the
follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

73
00:03:48,433 --> 00:03:52,380
Use the linked feature scripts for
the detailed screen recording plan.
